Rejected correctly at Step 0. The full [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.00606) shows:

- The proposed planted-color construction does not guarantee \(P_6\)-, diamond-, or \(K_4\)-freeness.
- Theorems 4–6 provide a polynomial certificate-producing coloring procedure, invalidating Track A.
- Track B also fails: DSATUR colored the tight 27-vertex example in a median 82.5 trials and 0.000225 seconds; the compact coordinate route requires comparable work.
- Scaling to 243 vertices still took only 0.0492 seconds, while any answer already requires 243 color entries.

The complete theorem analysis, mechanical-versus-compact measurements, and alternative families considered are recorded in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1703.00606/REJECTED.md). Per the task instructions, no generator or fabricated gate/oracle artifacts were created.
